# Milestone: M3
# Covers: when all strands are on the sleep queue (none on the ready queue),
#         sched_quiescent returns false (wakeup_pending_count > 0); after the
#         timer fires and strands are moved back to ready, quiescent stays false
#         until they finish, then becomes true.
#
# defer-to: T39
#
# Reason: observing the quiescence state machine from a chk fixture requires
# the ## host: mechanism to call sched_quiescent() directly and inspect VM
# internal counter state while strands are sleeping.  The chk runner is
# REPL-only; T39 is needed to wire host-driver assertions into chk fixtures.
# Additionally, time-literal/sleep primitives (T43) are needed to put a strand
# to sleep from urbiscript.
#
# When T39 + T43 land, implement this fixture by:
#   ## host: step VM; assert !sched_quiescent() while strand is sleeping
#   sleep(1ms)
#   ## host: advance clock, step; assert sched_quiescent() after completion
